    "The Amendment-10 opened-inode exclusion is applied only after parent._stable_record has read the complete opened bundle, manifest, or receipt bytes. The protected inode is rejected before torch deserialization, but it is not rejected before the first os.read; therefore a synthetic path switched to a production inode still opens and reads protected production bytes, and the committed regression that proves the late rejection cannot itself be run under the stricter unopened-production audit contract. The descriptor identity must be checked against every protected production role immediately after open/fstat and before the first read."
